    <string name="insight_s01_title">Recovery science</string>
    <string name="insight_s01_body">Without alcohol, REM sleep typically rebounds within the first two weeks — many people report dreaming vividly again.</string>

    <string name="insight_s02_title">Recovery science</string>
    <string name="insight_s02_body">Liver fat commonly starts reducing within two weeks of abstinence; enzyme markers like GGT often trend down within a month.</string>

    <string name="insight_s03_title">Recovery science</string>
    <string name="insight_s03_body">The brain\'s dopamine system typically takes 60–90 days to recalibrate after long-term drinking. Anhedonia in early weeks is common — and temporary.</string>

    <string name="insight_s04_title">Recovery science</string>
    <string name="insight_s04_body">Imaging studies often show measurable hippocampal recovery within a year of abstinence — short-term memory tends to improve along with it.</string>

